A. Commit message:
i2c: microchip-core: fix "ghost" detections

B. Change summary:
Removed the fast path that marks a message as complete when idev->msg_len is zero after sending a START/RESTART since this isn't a valid scenario. This prevents incorrect "ghost" detections during i2c-detect operations.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-microchip-corei2c.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-microchip-corei2c.c
index 6a124e903c666..5db73429125c0 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-microchip-corei2c.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-microchip-corei2c.c
@@ -287,8 +287,6 @@ static irqreturn_t mchp_corei2c_handle_isr(struct mchp_corei2c_dev *idev)
 		ctrl &= ~CTRL_STA;
 		writeb(idev->addr, idev->base + CORE_I2C_DATA);
 		writeb(ctrl, idev->base + CORE_I2C_CTRL);
-		if (idev->msg_len == 0)
-			finished = true;
 		break;
 	case STATUS_M_ARB_LOST:
 		idev->msg_err = -EAGAIN;
```